    {
      "paperId": "/chapter/10.1007/978-3-032-21960-2_3",
      "doi": "10.1007/978-3-032-21960-2_3",
      "title": "The Environment of Space as a Theater of War",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "Linda Dawson"
        }
      ],
      "year": 2026,
      "abstract": "A part of military strategy is to evaluate a theater of war for accessibility, affordability, and appropriateness for military operations. Considering outer space as a theater of war introduces a whole new set of parameters in order to deal with such a dangerous and unforgiving environment. Humans and spacecraft traveling in the extremes found in outer space need protection. Spacecraft need to be fabricated from materials that can tolerate the extreme temperatures and radiation. Because human life cannot naturally exist in outer space, artificial environments are necessary to provide life support for humans. This chapter focuses on the major issues affecting military operations in outer space, and how space as a military theater compares to a traditional war scenario.",
      "abstract_not_available": false,
